Platinum Rift - Episode 2: the map heights of the game CodinGame runs today, on "Referees/Platinum Rift2/Referee.java" of
https://github.com/SpiritusSancti5/codinGame (c0cc6fe). Applied by legacy/build.sh for the output name
cg-2014-platinum-rift-episode-2; the file as published is built as cg-2014-platinum-rift-episode-2-original.

The only change: MAX_HEIGHT 12 (the file: 18), i.e. a random map has 5 to 11 rows (random.nextInt(MAX_HEIGHT - MIN_HEIGHT)
+ MIN_HEIGHT; the file: 5 to 17), and 32/18 as many columns (8 to 19, 20 when symmetric). Inferred from CodinGame's public
replays (gameResult/findByGameId: 625 games of the top 1000 players; the game has a single division): their configuration
(the referee's getConfiguration()) shows a height of 5 to 11 in all 308 random maps, each equal to nextInt(7) + 5 drawn
where the file draws nextInt(13) + 5 from java.util.Random(seed); procedural, distribution and the fixed map are always
what the seed draws. The jar built with this patch reproduces all 625 replays frame for frame (views but for the order of
the visible zones, an identity hash order; infos, tooltips, scores) from the seed and the init property "symmetric"; the
file as published reproduces 340 of them (its other heights give other maps).

Not changed here: CodinGame passes "symmetric" itself (true in 271 of the 625 games, independent of the seed: it matches
the seed's own draw in about half of them), which the jar's CLI cannot pass (it passes only the seed): the referee then
draws it from the seed (true in half of the games).

diff --git a/Referees/Platinum Rift2/Referee.java b/Referees/Platinum Rift2/Referee.java
